it's cuba's most celebrated anniversary  the failed attack on the moncada  military barracks by fidel and raul  castro which marked the start of the  cuban revolution  69 years later raul castro now 91 still  appears to be going strong  but it's his successor miguel diaz canel  who must deal with escalating  disenchantment with the revolution  the imperial logic is betting on amnesia  of our history and social paralysis they  are betting the material needs provoked  by 63 years of their infamous blockade  will break the spirit of resistance of  our people  he was of course referring to the  world's longest economic embargo  imposed on cuba by the united states  cuba is undergoing its worst economic  crisis in 30 years power blackouts this  month in the middle of the stifling  summer have led to street protests  [Applause]  while tens of thousands of cubans are  fleeing  diaz canel continues to argue that the  u.s economic embargo is the root of all  of cuba's woes but on this occasion he  issued a novel challenge to the united  states  we conclude that they maintain their  blockade because without it our country  would be a model of a humane society too  subversive for the current world order  if i'm wrong then lift the blockade  immediately completely and without  restrictions and remove our so-called  pretext  in the meantime diaz canel promised that  in a few weeks he'll announce the  details of an economic reactivation plan  to counter acute shortages of food  supplies and energy  he ended the ceremony with the  traditional though increasingly  questioned cry of socialism and  fatherland or death  [Music]  lucian newman al jazeera
 

